contentText:
Music has a way of moving us before we even realize it—shifting a mood, unlocking a&nbsp;memory&nbsp;or changing the energy of a moment. The Planet Fitness Movement Mixes&nbsp;celebrate&nbsp;that instinctive connection, bringing together the songs that inspire us to move forward, find our&nbsp;rhythm&nbsp;and show up with intention.&nbsp;

For this talent-driven edition, Philadelphia-born singer,&nbsp;songwriter&nbsp;and producer Pink Sweat$ takes control of the playlist. Known for pairing intimate storytelling with stripped-back R&B, his music finds power in vulnerability—favoring warm vocals, rich&nbsp;melodies&nbsp;and emotional honesty over excess. Those same qualities shape a mix rooted in his musical world: Philadelphia soul, timeless R&B, funk,&nbsp;hip-hop&nbsp;and records built to make movement feel effortless.&nbsp;

The playlist unfolds like a complete workout. Jill Scott and Musiq Soulchild bring the warmth; The Roots and&nbsp;Anderson .Paak&nbsp;tighten the rhythm; Beyoncé, Meek Mill and Kendrick Lamar drive the intensity; and Frank Ocean, Sade and Bill Withers guide the body toward a softer landing. Pink Sweat$’ own “Icy” and “At My Worst” bookend two different sides of his artistry—from confident energy to tender reflection.&nbsp;

More than a collection of favorites, the mix offers a glimpse into the musical roots and influences behind Pink Sweat$’ sound.&nbsp;It moves across eras without losing its center, tracing the soul, groove and lyrical intention that have long defined Philadelphia music—and continue to inform his own approach.&nbsp;

Press play on  Pink Sweat$’ Movement Mix  and keep moving with Planet Fitness.

